# Development, Testing, and Use Instructions for Latent-UAD

## 1. Purpose

The goal is to make UAD less data-hungry by learning a compact latent representation of the domain before applying UAD-style structure discovery.

The learned representation should not merely reconstruct or predict the raw trace. It should preserve the kinds of structure UAD needs:

* persistent internal state,
* action-like variables,
* sensory interfaces,
* directed influence between subsystems,
* approximate separating boundaries,
* tolerable residual leakage,
* episodic emergence and disappearance of agentic structure.

The working hypothesis is:

[
X_t \rightarrow Z_t
]

where (X_t) is the raw observed trace and (Z_t) is a lower-dimensional latent slot representation on which UAD can operate with fewer samples.

The practical objective is not to discover perfect Markov blankets. It is to discover useful (\varepsilon)-blankets or optimal separating clusters:

[
C^\star = \arg\min_C \left[ \mathrm{Leakage}(C) + \lambda,\mathrm{Complexity}(C) - \mu,\mathrm{AgencyEvidence}(C) \right].
]

A good cluster is one where most relevant cross-boundary dependence is routed through a compact sensory/action interface, not one where all dependence vanishes.

